<h1>Tools</h1>

<p class="lede">Four tools, each on a page of its own. Each result follows its form as you change it, and a summary stays in view while you do, where the screen is tall enough. None of them is a personal forecast or a benefits check.</p>

<dl class="tool-list">
  <div><dt><a href="/tools/triple-lock/">Triple lock calculator</a></dt> <dd>How the triple lock chose each year's increase since April 2011, or what it would give for figures you choose.</dd></div>
  <div><dt><a href="/tools/compare/">Compare the rules for the yearly increase</a></dt> <dd>Five rules for the yearly increase, including the rule announced for April 2030, applied to the same figures.</dd></div>
  <div><dt><a href="/tools/budget/">Budget explorer: what does the pension cover?</a></dt> <dd>A household's income and spending, from your own figures or a research budget. Nothing you enter leaves your device.</dd></div>
  <div><dt><a href="/tools/history/">State Pension history explorer</a></dt> <dd>The full rates since 2010 as a chart and table, in cash, in buying power or against earnings.</dd></div>
</dl>

<p>To check your own State Pension, use GOV.UK: <a href="https://www.gov.uk/check-state-pension">check your State Pension forecast</a>.</p>
